    220
  ],
  "rules": [
    "Consume physical feed from the dated producer once, including whatever initial provisioning its declared boundary includes. Population does not multiply mining throughput in this consumer.",
    "The two catalogue tiers are disjoint. Summing the complete broad and narrow masses would double-count the narrow set.",
    "Track each year's requested, hypothetically supplied and unallocated feed. Unallocated demand is not silently imported or recovered from a fictional source.",
    "The accessible fraction limits raw feed. Product grade, recovery, quality and recycling belong in the physical producer and are not multiplied into inventory consumption a second time.",
    "A source-inventory pass only meets the stated hypothetical mass budget. It proves neither composition, route availability, mining approval, extraction capability nor economic reserves.",
    "Grade and recovery sensitivities must be supplied as physical reruns with actual feed, processing, equipment and transport responses. This consumer imposes no multiplier on an economy's operating or capital costs."
  ],
